# Session 14: the whole system through the gateway (docker compose up -d --build first).
# Everything goes to port 8000. Run top to bottom in IntelliJ or VS Code REST Client.

### 1. The gateway is alive
GET http://localhost:8000/actuator/health

### 2. The Task API answers through the gateway: look at the X-Served-By response header
GET http://localhost:8000/v3/api-docs

### 3. Log in as Sara (through the gateway, to the Task API)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "sara@flairs.dev", "password": "secret123"}

> {% client.global.set("sara", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 4. Stats: the first call runs SQL, the second comes from Redis (watch the task-api log: no SQL the 2nd time)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/tasks/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 5. Create a task: saved in PostgreSQL, stats evicted, task.created sent to RabbitMQ
POST http://localhost:8000/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Ship it with Docker", "priority": "HIGH", "projectId": 1}

> {% client.global.set("taskId", response.body.id); %}

### 6. Complete it: task.completed sent
PATCH http://localhost:8000/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 7. The notification service heard both (same token, a different service)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 8. No token: 401 from the notification service itself (the gateway does not check tokens)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/notifications

### 9. Not routed: 404 from the gateway
GET http://localhost:8000/internal/anything
